## Proposed Changes

---

### 1. [MODIFY] `templates/signup.html`

**Location:** Lines 115–123 (Submit button area)

**Current code:**
```html
<!-- Register Button -->
<button type="submit" class="submit-btn">
    <span>Register Account</span>
    <svg class="arrow-icon" ...> ... </svg>
</button>
```

**Replace with (add Cancel button below submit):**
```html
<!-- Register Button -->
<button type="submit" class="submit-btn" id="signup-submit-btn">
    <span>Register Account</span>
    <svg class="arrow-icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
        stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line>
        <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"></polyline>
    </svg>
</button>

<!-- FR 12: Cancel Button -->
<a href="{{ url_for('index') }}"
   class="cancel-btn"
   id="signup-cancel-btn"
   onclick="clearSignupForm()">
    Cancel
</a>
```

**Also add the JS function** before `</body>`:
```html
<script>
function clearSignupForm() {
    // Clear all form fields before navigating away
    var form = document.getElementById('signup-form');
    if (form) form.reset();
}
</script>
```

> **Why `<a>` not `<button>`?** Cancel redirects to another page — `<a href>` is semantically correct. `onclick` clears fields before navigation.

